{"The game on board no.7 was a very empty affair, for Mr Varley in defending a Scotch Game got his Kt embayed on K's 6 [actually e4], and having no road open to escape it was lost on the 12th move, and with this advantage winning was easy for Mr Weatherall. Source: BCM, April 1894, p150} 1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. d4 exd4 4. Nxd4 Nxd4 5. Qxd4 Nf6 6. e5 c5 7. Qd1 Ne4 8. Qe2 Qa5+ 9. c3 Qa4 10. b3 Qc6 11. f3 Nxc3 12. Nxc3 {and White won (32 moves). Source: Chess Monthly, Vol. 15, p245} 1-0

